en key (`progressTo"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/tools.md", "line": 13, "text": "Every tool and widget resource is registered through two local helpers, `_tool(...)` and `_resource(uri, ...)`, which wrap the function in `_tool_errors` / `_re"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/tools.md", "line": 290, "text": "- The tool body returns a `CallToolResult` carrying the Markdown as text content **and** a `_meta` dict assembled from four conditional keys plus one unconditio"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/tools.md", "line": 378, "text": "- `server.py` catches `AgentRunError`. With `agent.show_conversation_footer` on (the default): when `.agent_trace` is not `None` it returns a `CallToolResult(is"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/tools.md", "line": 537, "text": "The three `ui://` widget resources get the matching `_resource_errors(uri)` wrapper: an `Exception` other than `ResourceError` or `MCPError` is re-raised as `Re"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "line": 34, "text": "The CLI defends against this by routing every operator-facing error through a dedicated `err_console = Console(stderr=True)` defined at module scope in [src/sql"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "line": 41, "text": "Success/data output stays on stdout \u2014 `sqllens version`, `Wrote <path>` from `init`, `Config OK` + the validate summary, and the installer's `format_install_res"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "line": 80, "text": "- `_build_asgi_app_bare(cfg, readiness) -> tuple[ASGIApp, MCPServer]` is a private helper that returns the path-normalized + host-validated + authenticated app "}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "line": 86, "text": "MCPServer registers its endpoint at the **bare** path `/mcp`. Every MCP client we care about (Cursor, Claude Desktop, MCP Inspector) configures URLs ending in `"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "line": 167, "text": "Separately, the SDK rejects non-loopback `Host` headers with HTTP 421 (\"Misdirected Request\") \u2014 its own DNS-rebinding defense, which bites when running SQL Lens"}, {"file": "src/sqllens/server.py", "line": 255, "text": "# namespace the 2026-07-28 protocol stamps onto every request."}, {"file": "src/sqllens/server.py", "line": 264, "text": "``_meta`` object, which mcp 2.x exposes as a plain dict. Every key is"}, {"file": "src/sqllens/server.py", "line": 310, "text": "for key, value in meta.items()"}, {"file": "src/sqllens/server.py", "line": 318, "text": "if len(forwarded) > 64:"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py", "line": 165, "text": "assert not result.is_error"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py", "line": 190, "text": "assert not any(result.is_error for result in results)"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_stdio_serve.py", "line": 14, "text": "async def test_serve_over_stdio_lists_and_calls_tools(tmp_path: Path) -> None:"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_stdio_serve.py", "line": 16, "text": "key: value for key, value in os.environ.items() if not key.startswith(\"SQLLENS_\")"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_stdio_serve.py", "line": 37, "text": "assert {tool.name for tool in tools.tools} == {\"query_database\", \"list_data_sources\"}"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_stdio_serve.py", "line": 38, "text": "assert result.is_error is False"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_mcp_sdk_contract.py", "line": 66, "text": "return \"\".join(getattr(block, \"text\", \"\") for block in result.content)"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_mcp_sdk_contract.py", "line": 70, "text": "return {key for key in (result.meta or {}) if key.startswith(\"sqllens/\")}"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_mcp_sdk_contract.py", "line": 73, "text": "def _patch_impl(monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, impl) -> None:"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_mcp_sdk_contract.py", "line": 96, "text": ") -> None:"}], "audit_hints_truncated": true, "views": {"head": {"dir": ".prflow/tmp/rev